line: -Xlint:all, -g, -parameters, --enable-preview ...), stored as javac's own option processing stores them (its
Arguments needs classes TeaVM's class library lacks); the compiler had none, so warnings could not be turned on and
preview features not tried. After compiling, the deferred diagnostics are reported, as javac does when it closes:
the notes "Note: Main.java uses unchecked or unsafe operations." were never shown.

